From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm: process IRQ sources and return host state once

The VF2 SM's timer and software-interrupt paths were written when
sbi_sm_stop_enclave() ended in the non-returning sbi_trap_exit(). The
OpenSBI 1.6 port returns normally after replacing the trap register context,
which made the legacy post-call assignments reachable.

sbi_sm_stop_enclave() already returns SBI_ERR_SM_ENCLAVE_INTERRUPTED in a0
and advances the restored host mepc past its RUN/RESUME ecall. Updating a0
again is redundant, while advancing mepc a second time skips one Linux
instruction and corrupts the observed sbiret value. Keep the pre-call mepc
adjustment because it compensates for the increment performed when the
enclave is subsequently resumed.

Use the OpenSBI 1.6 timer and IPI handlers after restoring host context.
Processing an IRQ before sbi_sm_stop_enclave() sets STIP/SSIP and then the
Keystone S-mode CSR swap saves that host interrupt as enclave state. Every
RESUME consequently restores the stale pending bit and immediately retraps.
Restore the host first, then publish its pending interrupt. Clearing MIP_MTIP
directly also does not acknowledge the platform timer source.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [VF2 compatibility for OpenSBI 1.6]
---
 src/sbi_trap_hack.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sbi_trap_hack.c b/src/sbi_trap_hack.c
index c392a3d..72742c8 100644
--- a/src/sbi_trap_hack.c
+++ b/src/sbi_trap_hack.c
@@ -100,15 +100,13 @@ void sbi_trap_handler_keystone_enclave(struct sbi_trap_context *tcntx)
		case IRQ_M_TIMER: {
       regs->mepc -= 4;
       sbi_sm_stop_enclave(regs, STOP_TIMER_INTERRUPT);
+      sbi_timer_process();
-      regs->a0 = SBI_ERR_SM_ENCLAVE_INTERRUPTED;
-      regs->mepc += 4;
 			break;
                       }
		case IRQ_M_SOFT: {
       regs->mepc -= 4;
       sbi_sm_stop_enclave(regs, STOP_TIMER_INTERRUPT);
+      sbi_ipi_process();
-      regs->a0 = SBI_ERR_SM_ENCLAVE_INTERRUPTED;
-      regs->mepc += 4;
 			break;
                      }
 		default:
-- 
